      "worked_solution": "Notice that the points $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ lie on the circle. From the diagram, the radius of the circle is $r=OC=16.$ \n\nTo find $AB,$ we first notice that\n\n$$\nAB=AO+OB.\n$$\n\nNow, $\\overset{―}{AO}$ and $\\overset{―}{OB}$ are both segments between the center of the circle and the circle itself. So, they are both radii of the circle, and because the radius is $16,$ we have \n\n$$\nAO=16,\\,OB=16.\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\nAB=AO+OB=16+16=32.\n$$",
